<p>McAllen hail damage claims are some of the most common property insurance claims in the Rio Grande Valley (RGV). NOAA Storm Events data for Hidalgo County shows that hail reports cluster heavily in April and May, and several storms have produced very large stones. On April 20, 2012, softball-size hail was reported at McAllen High School, and on April 21, 2023, up to an hour of continuous hail fell across southern Hidalgo County, with baseball-size stones reported near Peñitas and McCook. More recently, the May 8, 2025 supercell produced reports of hail up to 3 inches in north McAllen (<a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1263450" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NCEI event record</a>).</p>
<p>Hail damage is often harder to see than it looks. Bruised shingles, cracked tiles, and dented metal can be missed from the ground, and the full scope may only show up during a close roof inspection. This page explains what a hail claim usually involves, where disputes arise, and how a public adjuster in McAllen may help. For deeper background, see our <a href="/storm-history/">McAllen storm history</a> page.</p>

<h2>Types of Property Damage Covered by Hail Claims</h2>
<p>Hail is a named peril on most homeowners and commercial property policies, subject to deductibles, exclusions, and endorsements. Hail claims in McAllen frequently involve:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Roofs</strong> &ndash; composition shingles (granule loss, bruising, fractured mats), clay or concrete tile, metal panels, and low-slope commercial membranes. See our <a href="/services/roof-damage-insurance-claims/">roof damage claims</a> page.</li>
<li><strong>Windows and skylights</strong> &ndash; broken glass, damaged frames and screens.</li>
<li><strong>Exterior walls</strong> &ndash; spatter and chips on stucco, cracked vinyl or fiber cement siding, damaged trim.</li>
<li><strong>Soft metals and equipment</strong> &ndash; gutters, downspouts, roof vents, and condenser coil fins on AC units.</li>
<li><strong>Other structures</strong> &ndash; fences, carports, sheds, and metal outbuildings.</li>
<li><strong>Interior damage</strong> &ndash; water intrusion through broken windows or punctured roofing.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Typical Documentation for a Hail Damage Claim</h2>
<p>Good documentation ties the damage to a storm date and shows the full scope of repairs. Our <a href="/claim-documentation-checklist/">claim documentation checklist</a> covers this in more detail.</p>
